-- Creature sizes from the vanilla import (VMaNGOS display_scale1..4 -> creature_template_model.DisplayScale). VMaNGOS sends
-- display_scale as the creature's final size: the 1.12 client does not apply the model's own scale, so the server sends
-- CreatureDisplayInfo.CreatureModelScale x CreatureModelData.ModelScale when display_scale is 0 and display_scale instead
-- of it otherwise (Unit::GetScaleForDisplayId, Creature::ChooseDisplayId). The modern client multiplies DisplayScale by
-- those two scales itself, so a Ragged Young Wolf (705, display_scale 0.7, display 855 at 0.4) showed at 0.28 instead of
-- 0.7. Here DisplayScale = display_scale / (CreatureModelScale x ModelScale), from the 1.15.9.70576 DB2s; rows whose model
-- scale is 1 are already right. Melee reach follows (Creature::SetObjectScale). A display_scale of exactly 1 became 1 too
-- and cannot be told from 0 here, so those creatures keep the model's own size. Safe to run again.
